        "short_description": {
            "database_value": "The United States Olympic & Paralympic Committee (USOPC) serves as the National Olympic Committee and National Paralympic Committee for the U.S. Founded in 1894, it is headquartered in Colorado Springs, Colorado. The USOPC empowers Team USA athletes to achieve competitive excellence and well-being while promoting the Olympic and Paralympic movements in the country.\n\nThe organization fields U.S. teams for various international competitions, including the Olympic and Paralympic Games. It provides extensive support to elite athletes and National Governing Bodies (NGBs) through integrated sport performance teams, financial assistance, and health services. The USOPC also oversees U.S. city bids for hosting major events and promotes athlete rights and safety. With training centers in Colorado Springs and Lake Placid, the USOPC creates optimal environments for athlete development and performance. Its initiatives aim to inspire and unite through sport, with a vision for a more inclusive world.",
            "ai_value": "The U.S. Olympic & Paralympic Committee is a non-profit organization dedicated to empowering Team USA athletes to achieve sustained competitive excellence and well-being, while leading the U.S. Olympic and Paralympic movements."
